---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalContact from '../components/LegalContact.astro';

// WORKING BUSINESS DRAFT — NOT A SUBSTITUTE FOR LEGAL REVIEW.
// Have this reviewed by a US-licensed attorney before relying on it
// commercially. Deliberately generic on numbers: BUXENA has not published
// a fixed return window, cancellation fee, or restocking fee.
const sections = [
  { id: 'overview', title: 'Overview' },
  { id: 'standard', title: 'Standard (In-Stock) Products' },
  { id: 'special-order', title: 'Special-Order, Custom and Made-to-Order Products' },
  { id: 'before-shipment', title: 'Cancelling Before Shipment' },
  { id: 'in-production', title: 'Orders Already in Production or Shipped' },
  { id: 'condition', title: 'Condition of Returned Goods' },
  { id: 'return-shipping', title: 'Return Shipping Costs' },
  { id: 'damaged-incorrect', title: 'Damaged or Incorrect Goods' },
  { id: 'how-to', title: 'How to Start a Return or Cancellation' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to This Policy' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact Us' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Returns & Cancellations"
  description="BUXENA's policy on returning or cancelling an order, for standard and special-order products."
>
  <section class="band band--tight page-head">
    <div class="shell legal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Returns &amp; Cancellations</span>
      <h1 class="display measure--tight">Returns &amp; Cancellations Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal__updated">Last Updated: July 2026</p>
      <p class="lead measure">
        What's possible depends heavily on the type of order — whether it's
        a standard product, or something special-order or made to order —
        and how far along it is. This policy explains how that works.
      </p>
      <LegalContact />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="shell legal">
      <nav class="legal__toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
        <ol>
          {sections.map((s, i) => (
            <li><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{i + 1}. {s.title}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <div class="legal__body">
        <article id="overview">
          <h2>1. Overview</h2>
          <p>
            Because our products are large, often imported to order, and
            sometimes built to a specific configuration, returns and
            cancellations are handled case by case rather than under one
            fixed rule. Always contact us before returning anything — see
            Section 9.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="standard">
          <h2>2. Standard (In-Stock) Products</h2>
          <p>
            For products we hold as standard stock, contact us as soon as
            possible if you'd like to cancel or return your order. We'll
            confirm what's possible for your specific order, including any
            timing and condition requirements, in writing.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="special-order">
          <h2>3. Special-Order, Custom and Made-to-Order Products</h2>
          <p>
            Many of our sauna models are imported or produced specifically
            for your order. Once production has started, a special-order,
            custom, or made-to-order product may no longer be eligible for
            cancellation or return. We will tell you clearly at the time of
            order whether your configuration falls into this category, and
            what that means for cancellation.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="before-shipment">
          <h2>4. Cancelling Before Shipment</h2>
          <p>
            If you need to cancel before your order ships, contact us
            immediately at{' '}
            <a href="mailto:info@buxena.com">info@buxena.com</a>. Whether a
            cancellation fee applies — and how much — depends on how far
            along the order is (for example, whether production or customs
            clearance has already started) and will be confirmed with you
            directly rather than charged at a fixed, pre-set rate.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="in-production">
          <h2>5. Orders Already in Production or Shipped</h2>
          <p>
            Orders that are already in production, in transit, or delivered
            are more limited in what can be changed or cancelled. We will
            always tell you what your options actually are for your
            specific order rather than apply a blanket rule.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="condition">
          <h2>6. Condition of Returned Goods</h2>
          <p>
            Where a return is accepted, the product generally needs to be
            unused, in its original packaging where possible, and in
            resalable condition, unless the return is due to damage or a
            defect. We'll confirm the specific condition requirements for
            your return in writing before you send anything back.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="return-shipping">
          <h2>7. Return Shipping Costs</h2>
          <p>
            Who pays return freight depends on the reason for the return.
            Given the size of these products, return shipping can be a
            meaningful cost — we'll be upfront with you about it before you
            proceed. If we shipped the wrong item or it arrived damaged or
            defective, see Section 8.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="damaged-incorrect">
          <h2>8. Damaged or Incorrect Goods</h2>
          <p>
            If your order arrived damaged, defective, or different from
            what you ordered, contact us promptly — see our{' '}
            <a href="/shipping/">Shipping &amp; Delivery Policy</a> for how
            to report shipping damage. We'll work with you on a repair,
            replacement, or other resolution appropriate to the situation.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="how-to">
          <h2>9. How to Start a Return or Cancellation</h2>
          <p>
            Email <a href="mailto:info@buxena.com">info@buxena.com</a> with
            your order details and what you'd like to do. Please don't ship
            anything back before we've confirmed the details with you in
            writing — unauthorized returns may not be accepted.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="changes">
          <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy from time to time. We will revise the
            "Last Updated" date above whenever we make a material change.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="contact">
          <h2>11. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>Questions about a return or cancellation can be directed to:</p>
          <LegalContact />
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

